{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"certifiable":true,"criteria":[{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":202,"line_start":108,"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py"},"criterion":"`rebar bridge fsck`, `rebar bridge check-access` and `rebar bridge setup` are the primary documented spellings and all dispatch; the old spellings remain functional compatibility entrypoints","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":202,"line_start":175,"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py"},"criterion":"Each rename is proven to be BEHAVIOUR-PRESERVING, not a reimplementation","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":202,"line_start":184,"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_jira_onboard.py"},"criterion":"`bridge setup` calls `bridge check-access` as its FINAL validation step, still injecting the just-persisted settings as an env overlay, and still skipping the check when `JIRA_API_TOKEN` is unset (exit 0) or `--no-validate` is passed","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":119,"line_start":114,"path":"src/rebar/_cli/_bridge_commands.py"},"criterion":"`check-access` ships as its own primary verb — there is no `bridge fsck --check-access` flag spelling. The legacy `bridge-probe` compatibility entrypoint routes to the same operation","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":5,"line_start":3,"path":"src/rebar/schemas/bridge_fsck.schema.json"},"criterion":"`src/rebar/schemas/bridge_fsck.schema.json` has BOTH its `$id` and its `description` updated to the new verb name","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":78,"line_start":78,"path":"tests/unit/test_canary_bridge_wiring.py"},"criterion":"Every consumer enumerated above is migrated in the same change. In particular the STRING-named sites are covered: `tests/unit/test_jira_onboard.py`'s `monkeypatch.setattr(\"rebar._cli._bridge_probe\", ...)` (3 sites) and `tests/unit/test_canary_bridge_wiring.py:78`'s literal `\"rebar bridge-fsck\"`","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":113,"line_start":1,"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py"},"criterion":"A test greps current docs, workflow invocations, and primary help for stale uses of `bridge-fsck`, `bridge-probe`, or `jira-onboard`, while explicitly allowing the compatibility registrations, parity tests, release/migration notes, CHANGELOG, `docs/archive`, and ADR history","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":509,"line_start":500,"path":"scripts/canary_bridge.py"},"criterion":"`scripts/canary_bridge.py` and `.github/workflows/reconcile-bridge-canary.yml` invoke the new verb, and the canary still classifies binding drift identically","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":162,"line_start":149,"path":"tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py"},"criterion":"`scripts/gen_cli_reference.py` + `tests/unit/test_gen_cli_reference.py` are updated together and the regenerated `docs/cli-reference.md` matches","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"kind":"file","line_end":123,"line_start":115,"path":"tests/interfaces/contracts/test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py"},"criterion":"The library and MCP `bridge_fsck` entrypoints are UNCHANGED by this ticket and still callable at its boundary","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true},{"citation":{"description":"Ticket comment confirms docs/release-notes.md lines 11-21 record all three mappings with canonical/compatibility distinction. test_bridge_vocabulary_stale_heldout.py lines 103-112 asserts this programmatically.","kind":"source"},"criterion":"Release notes record all three old -> new mappings, identify the new spellings as primary, and document that the old spellings remain supported compatibility entrypoints for continuity","kind":"codebase-verifiable","met":true}],"findings":[],"material_fingerprint":null,"metrics":{"det_ms":1490.7,"llm_calls":1,"llm_ms":193250.5,"requests":43,"tool_calls":43,"total_ms":194776.1},"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider_provenance":{"capabilities":{"native_structured_output":true,"prompt_cache_style":"bedrock","supports_temperature":true,"supports_thinking":true,"web_access":"off"},"endpoint_host":null,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6","provider":"bedrock","tier":"first_class"},"runner":"pydantic_ai","schema":"completion_verifier_pass_v1","ticket_id":"e27c-5a20-cd13-43b2","trace_id":null,"verdict":"PASS","verified_at_sha":"71c27f91db29f25c5269d1d1cb5cadecbc8a5ccf"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMPLETION_VERDICT","timestamp":1786359131881854001,"uuid":"a8013189-9645-496d-a0ab-2c0a1d730af6"}